<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Hanover</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1692–1866</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanover">Hanover</a> was a German princely dynasty, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-elector">electors</a> and later kings of Hanover, that ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-great-britain">Great Britain</a> and Ireland from 1714 to 1901. The English <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/act-of-settlement-1701">Act of Settlement</a> of 1701 fixed the succession on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sophia-of-hanover">Sophia of Hanover</a>, a Protestant granddaughter of James I, and her son became George I in 1714. The personal union with Hanover ended at Victoria's accession in 1837.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-hanover.jpg" alt="House of Hanover" width="320" height="374" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Royal_Arms_of_the_Kingdom_of_Hanover.svg: Sodacan derivative work: Sodacan (talk) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Royal_Hanover_Inescutcheon.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
